@preamble use("turtle/simple")
new
@unchecked
Initializes the drawing environment and places the turtle at its home position.
With no argument the canvas is 800 by 800 pixels; with dim, a square canvas of
dim by dim pixels is used and that size is remembered.
The window appears when this is called. If the window is closed, calling new
again starts a fresh session.
A newly initialized turtle is at logical position [0, 0], has heading 0, has its
pen down, uses color :white, and is visible.

new(dim)

use("turtle/simple")
new(800)
forward(50)
===
logical
@unchecked
Sets the width and height of the logical coordinate space to size.
The default is 200, giving coordinate bounds from -100 through 100 along each
axis. The origin is at the center of the canvas, positive x extends to the
right, and positive y extends upward.
Changing the logical size changes the mapping between logical units and pixels
but does not change the turtle's logical position.

logical(size)

new(800)
logical(100)    # coordinates now range from -50 through 50
===
forward
@unchecked
Moves the turtle forward by distance logical units in its current heading.
Draws a line if the pen is down; otherwise only the position changes.
Movement is clamped to the logical bounds: a movement that would pass beyond an
edge stops at that edge.

forward(distance)

forward(50)
===
backward
@unchecked
Moves the turtle backward by distance logical units, in the direction opposite
its current heading.

backward(distance)

backward(25)
===
left
@unchecked
Decreases the current heading by angle degrees.

left(angle)

left(90)
===
right
@unchecked
Increases the current heading by angle degrees.
Heading 0 points upward and 90 points to the right.

right(angle)

right(90)
heading()    # 90
===
pen_up
@unchecked
Lifts the pen, so subsequent movement changes position without drawing.

pen_up()

pen_up()
forward(20)    # moves without drawing
===
pen_down
@unchecked
Lowers the pen, so subsequent movement draws.

pen_down()

pen_down()
forward(20)    # draws a line
===
pen_size
@unchecked
Sets the drawing width in logical units.
The value is scaled to the current canvas; the resulting pixel width is never
less than one pixel.

pen_size(n)

pen_size(3)
===
pencolor
@unchecked
Sets the color used for subsequent turtle drawing.
A color may be a symbol such as :red, or a list of red, green, and blue
components with an optional alpha component.

pencolor(color)

pencolor(:red)
pencolor([30, 144, 255])
===
background
@unchecked
Sets the canvas background color.
A color may be a symbol or a list of components, as for pencolor.

background(color)

background(:black)
===
show_turtle
@unchecked
Displays the turtle indicator on the canvas.
Visibility affects only the indicator; it does not affect movement or drawing.

show_turtle()

show_turtle()
===
hide_turtle
@unchecked
Removes the turtle indicator from view.
Visibility affects only the indicator; it does not affect movement or drawing.

hide_turtle()

hide_turtle()
===
home
@unchecked
Moves the turtle to [0, 0] and resets its heading to 0.
Returning home does not draw a line, regardless of the current pen state.
The pen state and drawing color are preserved.

home()

home()
===
clear
@unchecked
Clears the canvas using its current background color.
The turtle's position, heading, pen state, color, and visibility are unchanged.

clear()

clear()
===
position
@unchecked
Returns the current logical position as a shaped point [@point, x, y].
The reported coordinates are truncated to integers.

position()

home()
position()    # [@point, 0, 0]
===
heading
@unchecked
Returns the current heading in degrees.
Heading 0 points upward and 90 points to the right.

heading()

home()
right(90)
heading()    # 90
